b. Write a HTML program to explain the working of hyperlinks using <a> tag and href, target
attributes.
Note: Use text to link → https://www.aec.edu.in/
Use image to link → https://www.aec.edu.in/?p=Gallery
<a> Tag (Anchor Tag)
 The <a> tag is used to create hyperlinks in HTML.
 Anything inside the <a> tag (text, image, or other content) becomes clickable.
 Syntax:
<a href="URL">Clickable Text or Image</a>
href Attribute (Hypertext Reference)
 The href attribute specifies the URL of the page or resource you want to link to.
 Example:
<a href="https://www.aec.edu.in/">Visit AEC</a>
 Without href, the <a> tag won’t link anywhere.
target Attribute
 The target attribute defines where to open the linked page.
 Common values:
o _blank → Opens the link in a new tab or window.
o _self → Opens the link in the same tab (default).
 Example:
<a href="https://www.aec.edu.in/" target="_blank">AEC Website</a>
 <a> → creates a link
 href → tells the link where to go
 target → tells where to open the link
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
